# Wrath of God destroys Aang, at the Crossroads and Bot1's Ornithopter at once. A leaves-the-battlefield ability looks back
# (CR 603.10a): Aang's triggers for the Ornithopter, another creature Bot1 controlled, though Aang left with it - but not for
# Aang himself, who is no "another creature", so there is one trigger, not two. Its delayed ability triggers at Bot2's upkeep
# on turn 4 and finds no Aang to transform (he is a card in the graveyard, a new object, CR 400.7): the stack empties and
# nothing comes back.

